[{"page":1,"text":"NOTICE OF A REGULAR\n\nPLANNING COMMISSION MEETING\n\nMay 6, 2026, at 7:00 PM\n________________\nPUBLIC NOTICE is hereby given that the Vineyard Planning Commission will hold a regularly\nscheduled Planning Commission meeting on Wednesday, May 6, 2026, at 7:00 PM, in the City\nCouncil Chambers at City Hall, 125 South Main Street, Vineyard, UT. This meeting can also be\nviewed on our live stream page.\n\n1.\n\nCALL TO ORDER/INVOCATION/INSPIRATIONAL THOUGHT/PLEDGE OF\n\nALLEGIANCE\n\n2.\n\nPRESENTATIONS/RECOGNITIONS/AWARDS/PROCLAMATIONS\n\n3.\n\nPUBLIC COMMENTS PC\nTime dedicated for public comment. Comments will be limited to three (3) minutes. No\nactions may be taken by the Planning Commission due to the need for proper public\nnoticing. Public comments can be submitted ahead of time to planning@vineyardutah.gov.\n\n4.\n\nCONSENT ITEMS\n\n5.\n\nBUSINESS ITEMS\n\n5.1. Chair and Vice-Chair Re-election\n\nThe Commission will nominate and then elect the standing Chair and Vice-Chair\npositions for the 2026 calendar year.\n\n5.2. Conditional Use and Site Plan Application- Tire Auto Body Shop and Retail at\n\n430 S Geneva Road, Regional Commercial Zone\n\nGuilford Rand requests approval of a site plan for a two-building commercial\ndevelopment at 430 S Geneva Road in the Regional Commercial Zone, including a\ntire/auto body shop, general retail space, restaurant, parking, landscaping, and related\nsite improvements.\n\n5.3. Site Plan Amendment: Utah City Wellness Center and Resort Pool Phase 2\n\nFlagborough requests approval of a site plan amendment for Utah City Wellness\nCenter and Resort Pool Phase 2 to update building elevations and landscaping, with no\nother changes to the previously approved site plan.\n\n6.\n\nWORK SESSION\n\n6.4. Floodplain Regulation Update, National Flood Insurance Program (NFIP)\n\nPage 1 of 2; May 6, 2026, Planning Commission Agenda\nPage 1 of 122","ocr":false},{"page":2,"text":"Compliance\n\nUpdates to the City’s floodplain management ordinance are required to maintain\ncompliance with the National Flood Insurance Program (NFIP) following updated\n\nFEMA flood hazard determinations.\n\n7.\n\nSTAFF AND COMMISSION REPORTS\n\n8.\n\nADJOURNMENT\n\nThe next regularly scheduled meeting is on May 20, 2026\nThe public is invited to participate in all Planning Commission meetings. In compliance with the\nAmericans with Disabilities Act, individuals needing special accommodations during this public\nmeeting should notify the planning staff at least 24 hours prior to the meeting by calling (801)\n\n226-1929 or email at planning@vineyardutah.gov.\nThe foregoing notice and agenda were posted on the Utah Public Notice Website and Vineyard\nWebsite, posted at Vineyard City Hall, and delivered electronically to city staff and each member\nof the Planning Commission.\n\nMay 1, 2026\n\nAGENDA NOTICING COMPLETED ON:\n\n/s/ Rachel Stevens\n\nCERTIFIED (NOTICED) BY:\n\nPage 2 of 2; May 6, 2026, Planning Commission Agenda\nPage 2 of 122","ocr":false},{"page":3,"text":"VINEYARD CITY COUNCIL STAFF REPORT\n\nMeeting Date: May 6, 2026\nAgenda Item: Conditional Use and Site Plan Application- Tire Auto Body Shop and Retail at\n\n430 S Geneva Road, Regional Commercial Zone\n\nDepartment:\n\nPresenter:\n\nCommunity Development\n\nAnthony Fletcher\n\nBackground/Discussion:\nGuilford Rand, representing Angela Castro, has submitted a site plan application for the\ndevelopment of property located at 430 S Geneva Road. The property is located within the\n\nRegional Commercial (RC) Zone. The proposed development includes two commercial\nbuildings intended to accommodate a tire/auto body shop, general retail space, and a restaurant.\nThe tire and auto body shop would be classified as Vehicle and Equipment Repair (Minor),\nwhich is a conditional use within the RC Zone.\nVehicle and Equipment Repair is defined as an establishment providing motor vehicle repair or\nmaintenance services conducted entirely within completely enclosed buildings. See Vineyard\nZoning Code Section 15.60.020. Typical uses include electronic tune-ups, brake repairs, air\nconditioning repairs, generator and starter repairs, tire repairs, front-end alignments, battery\nrecharging, lubrication, and the sale, repair, and installation of minor parts and accessories such\nas tires, batteries, windshield wipers, hoses, and windows. Vehicle and Equipment Repair\n(Minor) may also include the retail sale of fuels, lubricants, and other motor vehicle supplies.\nBuilding A is proposed to be 19,712 square feet. Building B is proposed to be 8,200 square feet.\nThe majority of the development is single-story; however, Building A includes a second-story\nretail area and a basement for storage. The maximum proposed building height for Building A is\n30 feet 2 inches, and the maximum proposed building height for Building B is 27 feet 6 inches.\nBoth buildings are below the maximum building height of 60 feet allowed in the RC Zone.\nThe site plan meets the minimum parking requirement. The table below shows the parking\nrequirements and total count.\n\nFormula per Vineyard Spaces\n\nCity Code 15.38.030 Required\n\n1 space per 1,000 sq ft 2\n\nUse\n\nArea\n\nWarehouse /\n\nStorage\n\nRestaurant\n\n2,198\n\nSF\n\n2,000 1 space per 100 sq ft\n\nSF\n\n1,000 1 space per 200 sq ft\n\nSF\n\n8 bays 3 spaces per bay\n\n20,078 1 space per 250 sq ft\n\nSF\n\nKitchen\n\nTire Repair\n\nRetail\n\nSpaces\n\nProvided\n\nADA Spaces per\n\nIBC Table 1106.1\n\n20\n\n5\n\n24\n\n80\n\nPage 3 of 122","ocr":false},{"page":4,"text":"Total Vehicle —\n\nParking\n\nBicycle Parking —\n\n—\n\n131\n\n131\n\n10% of required parking 13\n\n13\n\n5 required / 6\nprovided\n—\n\nThe proposed site plan includes two commercial buildings with associated parking, landscaping,\nand site improvements. The proposed building materials include wood and stucco. The north and\neast facades of Building B will feature a mural near the corner of 400 South and Geneva Road.\nThe mural will help beautify the intersection, which is a key entrance into Vineyard City. The\nsubmitted building elevations have been reviewed for compliance with the applicable\nrequirements of the Vineyard Zoning Code.\nVineyard Zoning Code Section 15.40 requires at least one tree for every 20 feet of street frontage\nand requires 20% of the total area to be landscaped. The landscape plan proposes a total of 51\ntrees of various species and 21% of the total area landscaped. The landscaping areas are\nproposed to be finished with crushed rock. The proposed landscaping plan meets the applicable\nrequirements.\nThe proposed site plan is consistent with the Regional Commercial Zone and is intended to\nsupport commercial uses along Geneva Road. The proposed mix of uses, including auto-related\nservices, general retail, and restaurant space, is compatible with the purpose of the RC Zone.\nIt is important to note that Engineering has restricted the applicant’s access on 400 South to\nright-in/right-out only, with a traffic barrier to prevent illegal turns into and out of the proposed\ndevelopment.\nStaff finds that the proposed site layout, building elevations, parking, and landscaping are\nconsistent with the applicable provisions of the Vineyard Zoning Code.\n\nFiscal Impact:\n\nThere is no fiscal impact.\n\nRecommendation:\nStaff recommends approval of the site plan application and conditional use permit for the\nproposed tire/auto body shop, general retail, and restaurant development located at 430 S Geneva\n\nRoad, subject to the following conditions:\n\n1. The applicant pays any outstanding fees and makes any redline corrections.\n\n2. The applicant is subject to all federal, state, and local laws.\n\n3. All vehicle repairs shall be conducted entirely within an enclosed space.\n\nSample Motion:\n\"I move to approve the site plan application and conditional use permit for the proposed tire/auto\nbody shop, general retail, and restaurant development located at 430 S